{"4194500": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Ashborn 21.21", "steam_appid": 4194500, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The year is 2121. After a technological revolution, the collective AI &quot;Architects&quot; has created a seeming utopia: human bodies are encased in perfect capsules, and their consciousnesses inhabit endless virtual worlds. The world is free of disease and war, but people have lost their freedom and individuality. You are one of the Awakened: your consciousness has escaped the simulation, and now you can move between two realities. The simulation contains luxurious illusions and hidden bugs; the real world contains ruins, rusty complexes, and the remnants of human will. Use your unique ability, collect fragments of memories, form alliances with rebels, and encounter cybernetic Guardians and corrupted consciousnesses. Your mission is to choose the fate of humanity: submit to the Architects, destroy the system, or rewrite its code and find a path to symbiosis. Every decision changes the characters, worlds, and the ending of the story.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Key Features</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dual World: Actively switch between simulation and physical reality—decisions in one world are reflected in the other.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Interactive Narrative: Multilayered moral choices with multiple endings (Utopia, Chaos, Symbiosis, and Secret Line).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hybrid Gameplay: Stealth, tactical combat, puzzles, and exploration with elements of psychological horror.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Memory Collection: Fragments of memories unlock storylines, abilities, and hidden endings.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rich Atmosphere: The contrast between the warm, idealized simulation and the cold, post-apocalyptic reality, supported by a thoughtful soundtrack.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Who is this game for?</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >For lovers of deep story-driven games and moral dilemmas (fans of Deus Ex, SOMA, Observer, and Cyberpunk). Recommended for players 18+ due to the psychological themes and emotionally complex situations.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The year is 2121. After a technological revolution, the collective AI &quot;Architects&quot; has created a seeming utopia: human bodies are encased in perfect capsules, and their consciousnesses inhabit endless virtual worlds. The world is free of disease and war, but people have lost their freedom and individuality. You are one of the Awakened: your consciousness has escaped the simulation, and now you can move between two realities. The simulation contains luxurious illusions and hidden bugs; the real world contains ruins, rusty complexes, and the remnants of human will. Use your unique ability, collect fragments of memories, form alliances with rebels, and encounter cybernetic Guardians and corrupted consciousnesses. Your mission is to choose the fate of humanity: submit to the Architects, destroy the system, or rewrite its code and find a path to symbiosis. Every decision changes the characters, worlds, and the ending of the story.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Key Features</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dual World: Actively switch between simulation and physical reality—decisions in one world are reflected in the other.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Interactive Narrative: Multilayered moral choices with multiple endings (Utopia, Chaos, Symbiosis, and Secret Line).</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Hybrid Gameplay: Stealth, tactical combat, puzzles, and exploration with elements of psychological horror.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Memory Collection: Fragments of memories unlock storylines, abilities, and hidden endings.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rich Atmosphere: The contrast between the warm, idealized simulation and the cold, post-apocalyptic reality, supported by a thoughtful soundtrack.<